max-visits: 1

= The Serannus Plan and the fall of the coalition

The Foreign Ministry under Gustav Stratton has agreed to the Serannus Plan — an offer by an <span style="color: #002654;">Ethian</span> delegation to restructure the Commonwealth's War Loans and grant us greater fiscal autonomy, extended only because <span style="color: #002654;">Ethia</span> would sooner shore up a friendly, anti-Axton government than risk a Restorationist one taking its place. Simultaneously, <span style="color: #002654;">Ethia</span> will agree to withdraw its military occupation from the Exetar.

While this seems to be a positive development for the country, the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>, despite their moderation, oppose the plan — incensed that its relief passes over their own great landed estates — claiming that any War Loans are a form of national slavery. They have called for a vote of no confidence against the government, supported by the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span> (who would repudiate the War Loans outright),
<span style="color: #003755;">**CNF**</span> and the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span>, and for a referendum on the Serannus Plan.

We can either vote to bring down the government and hold new elections, or "tolerate" a government led by the remaining propertied parties.

- @vonc_yes
- @vonc_no
- @no_matter

@vonc_yes
title: Support the vote of no confidence, voting against the government.
subtitle: The government will collapse, and there will be new elections.
view-if: neo_weimar_coalition >= 50
on-arrival: time_to_election = 3; marcher_in_government = 0; in_right_coalition = 0; in_center_right_coalition = 0; in_grand_coalition = 0; marcher_toleration = 0; marcher_toleration_right = 0; gold_relation -= 3; unionist_relation -= 3; ddp_relation -= 3; lvp_relation -= 3; gold_right += 1; ddp_right += 0.5; lvp_right += 1
call: set_next_election_time
go-to: new_prussia_election if (in_center_right_coalition_heartland or in_right_coalition_heartland)

The <span style="color: #000000;">propertied</span>-<span style="color: #3E88B3;">right</span> coalition has fallen. New elections have been set for [+ next_election_month : month +] [+ next_election_year +].

@vonc_no
title: Support the rump [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?]-led government, voting in favor of the government.
subtitle: We would essentially provide "toleration" to a propertied government.
view-if: neo_weimar_coalition >= 50
on-arrival: marcher_toleration = 1; in_right_coalition = 0; in_center_right_coalition = 0; left_dissent += 8; ddp_left += 0.5
go-to: new_prussia_election if (in_center_right_coalition_heartland or in_right_coalition_heartland)

By supporting the government, we have essentially entered into a "toleration" arrangement with the [+ chancellor +] government. We do not have a voice in the government, but we are responsible for its continued stability. The left of our party opposes this plan, and would rather that we hold new elections.

@no_matter
title: It does not matter what we do.
subtitle: The anti-government parties have over 50% of the vote, no matter our choices.
view-if: neo_weimar_coalition < 50
call: set_next_election_time
on-arrival: time_to_election = 3; marcher_in_government = 0; in_right_coalition = 0; in_center_right_coalition = 0; in_grand_coalition = 0; marcher_toleration = 0; marcher_toleration_right = 0; pro_republic -= 5
go-to: new_prussia_election if (in_center_right_coalition_heartland or in_right_coalition_heartland)

The <span style="color: #000000;">propertied</span>-<span style="color: #3E88B3;">right</span> coalition has fallen. New elections have been set for [+ next_election_month : month +] [+ next_election_year +].

@new_prussia_election
on-arrival: heartland_coalition_trigger = 1

The Heartland coalition isn't able to survive either, pressure from the national conservatives within the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> forces them to exit from the <span style="color: #000000;">propertied</span>-<span style="color: #3E88B3;">right</span> coalition there as well.

- @prussian_coalition_formation: Negotiate a new Heartland coalition.
